          "date": "2026-11-19 19:07:17.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-19 19:21:02.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20904 ofd: no PFID check before a parent FID is stored",
        "message": "LU-20904 ofd: no PFID check before a parent FID is stored\n\nWith lfsck_verify_pfid enabled, the OST checks the parent FID that\na client sends with a write or punch against the one stored in the\nobject's filter_fid.  For a mirrored or EC file, the MDT stores the\nlayout version in the objects' filter_fid before the first write\ndoes, which leaves a filter_fid with no parent FID.  The OST would\ntake that as a mismatch and ask the MDT to verify the object,\nreturning -EINPROGRESS to the client meanwhile.  For a mirrored file\nthe MDT would confirm the object and the OST \"repair\" it.  For an EC\nfile the MDT would refuse the parity layout with -EOPNOTSUPP, so the\nobject was never verified, and the client would resend every I/O to\nthe file forever.\n\nTreat a filter_fid without a parent FID like a missing one: there\nis nothing to check, and the write stores the client's parent FID.\n\nAdd sanity-lfsck test_19c to write a mirrored and an EC file with\nlfsck_verify_pfid enabled.\n\nFixes: 10da8afb2786 (\"LU-9771 flr: Send write intent RPC to mdt\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lfsck\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I754d88270e1a41a9c0b0db2dd0dc8786ae3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
